WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.982
Sorting is useful when you want to quickly identify high, low, early, late, or otherwise important records.

00:00:07.982 --> 00:00:12.952
The sort values method can order the table using one or more columns.

00:00:12.952 --> 00:00:22.692
For a numeric column, the N largest method is a convenient way to return the highest values without manually sorting the

00:00:22.692 --> 00:00:29.667
entire table. For example, you might use it to find the five largest transactions, the highest-performing stores,

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:32.722
or the customers with the largest balances.

00:00:32.722 --> 00:00:37.432
Whenever you look at top records, also consider context.

00:00:37.432 --> 00:00:44.672
A very large value may represent strong performance, a rare event, or a data quality problem.

00:00:44.672 --> 00:00:49.588
Sorting helps us find the record; interpretation tells us what it means.
